{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And when HaShem sent, etc.</b> The meaning is: to Joshua and Caleb, to spy out the land — His intention was to say ״Go up and possess the land which I am giving״ etc., as He said in the portion of Shelach (Numbers 13:2): ״אֲשֶׁר אֲנִי נוֹתֵן״, and see what I explained there. And He interrupted the matter of the spies and the matter of Taberah and Massah etc. in the middle of the episode of the calf — He intended to place all the provocations adjacent to one another, for had the entire order of the episode of the calf been completed first, it would have created a great distance between one provocation and the next, and such a separation would produce a diminishment of the emotional impact toward which He aims."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:16:21.182147764Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}